{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Few and evil have been the days of the years of my life.</b> In response to your saying, <b>How many are the days of the years of your life?</b> — I say that the years of my life have been few and evil, due to the abundance of toil for sustenance and worries of hardships. For the days in which a man is in distress are not called days of the years of life, but <b>the days of the years of my sojournings</b> have been, all together, <b>a hundred and thirty years.</b>" "<b>And the days of the years of my life have not attained the days of the years of my fathers' lives in their sojournings.</b> For my fathers, even though they too were sojourners in a land not their own, nevertheless had many days of life without distress; but the years of my life have not attained the years of my fathers' lives which they had in the days of their sojournings."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:56.359519592Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}